      "name": "Jomon Sugi Cedar",
      "description": "Jomon Sugi is the oldest and most famous cedar tree on Yakushima, estimated at 2,170–7,200 years old, and considered a symbol of the island's UNESCO World Heritage ancient forest. Reaching it requires an 8–10 hour round-trip hike through the mystical moss-covered forest that inspired Studio Ghibli's Princess Mononoke.",
      "highlights": [
        "~7,200-year-old ancient cedar tree",
        "Epic 8-10h hike through UNESCO forest",
        "Inspiration for Princess Mononoke landscape"
      ],
      "openingHours": "Open 24 hours"
    },
    "ja": {
      "name": "縄文杉",
      "description": "縄文杉は屋久島を代表する最大最古の屋久杉で、推定樹齢2,170〜7,200年とされ、ユネスコ世界遺産の古代森林のシンボルです。スタジオジブリ『もののけ姫』の舞台にもなった苔むす神秘的な森の中を往復8〜10時間かけて訪ねるトレッキングは一生の思い出になります。",
      "highlights": [
        "推定樹齢7,000年の古代屋久杉",
